# Bring-up helper scripts (pc-stay-awake, pc-screencap, pc-debug-dump,
# pc-kmsg-file, pc-logcat-file).
#
# On system_ext, labelled shell_exec, so init's services run them in the shell
# domain -- init.te already carries domain_trans(init, shell_exec, shell), so no
# transition rule is needed.
#
# They cannot live on /vendor. They run screencap, logcat and ip, and a vendor
# domain may neither entrypoint from a coredomain nor execute system files:
#
#     neverallow coredomain { file_type -system_file_type ... }:file entrypoint;
#     # Do not allow vendor components to execute files from system
#     neverallow { domain -shell -ueventd ... } system_file:file execute;
#
# Nor can they sit on /system with the label declared in the device's vendor
# sepolicy, which is where this entry started:
#
#     ERROR: Vendor's file_contexts must not label files in platform partitions.
#     Violations: /system/bin/pc_[a-z_]+\.sh
#
# system_ext is the partition a device may add platform components to, and this
# file is its private policy (SYSTEM_EXT_PRIVATE_SEPOLICY_DIRS). Both spellings
# are matched because system_ext is folded into system/ on this product.
# device/google/cuttlefish/.../system_ext/private/file_contexts labels its own
# set_adb.sh the same way.
/(system_ext|system/system_ext)/bin/pc_[a-z_]+\.sh    u:object_r:shell_exec:s0
